## PROJECT: TaalDNA

A language-learning style assessment tool (UI in Dutch; works for any target language).
Users complete 4 interactive exercises (not questionnaires).
We measure behavior, not self-report.
Result: a 2D profile (Processing Style × Social Style) + honest app recommendations.

## TECH STACK
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- Framer Motion (animations)
- Shadcn/ui (components)
- Supabase (database + email capture)
- Vercel (deployment)

## DESIGN PRINCIPLES
- Mobile-first. Every screen must look great on iPhone.
- Clean, modern, Dutch language throughout.
- Animations should feel smooth, not flashy.
- Progress bar always visible during assessment.
- No clutter. One action per screen.

## THE 4 EXERCISES (core product)
1. Contextueel Raden — user guesses word from context (measures: analyse vs. intuïtie)
2. Luister en Schrijf — user hears audio, types what they hear (measures: auditieve verwerking)
3. 30 Seconden Split-Screen — timed interaction choice (measures: sociaal vs. solo)
4. Bouw de Zin (Drag & Drop) — user drags words into correct order (measures: systematisch vs. intuïtief)

## 2D PROFILE AXES
- X-axis: Analytisch ←→ Intuïtief
- Y-axis: Solo ←→ Sociaal

## APP RECOMMENDATIONS (honest, no marketing)
- Duolingo: goed voor intuïtieve, sociale leerders
- Anki: goed voor analytische, solo leerders
- Pimsleur: goed voor auditieve leerders
- Babbel: goed voor analytische, gestructureerde leerders
- italki: goed voor sociale leerders die echte gesprekken willen

## ROUTING
/ → Landing page
/start → Onboarding
/assessment → 4 oefeningen in volgorde
/resultaat → 2D profiel reveal + score
/aanbevelingen → App aanbevelingen op basis van profiel
/vergelijk/taaldna → TaalDNA vs. andere leerstijl-tools
/vergelijk/polycards → PolyCards vs. andere flashcard-apps
/bedankt → Email capture + bedankpagina

## CODE STYLE
- Always use TypeScript
- Component-based architecture
- Keep components small and focused
- Use Framer Motion for page transitions
- Show plan first, then execute

## 🔧 DEV SERVER MANAGEMENT

Before starting `npm run dev`, ALWAYS kill existing processes on ports 3000-3004:

```powershell
@(3000,3001,3002,3003,3004) | ForEach-Object {
  $p = Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort $_ -EA SilentlyContinue
  if ($p) { Stop-Process -Id $p.OwningProcess -Force }
}
```

Then clear the Next.js cache and start fresh:
```powershell
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .next -EA SilentlyContinue
npm run dev
```

NEVER start `npm run dev` without first killing existing port processes.
The dev server must always run on port 3000.
